# =============================================================================================
# Nothing of the game's own goes in this repository.
#
# This project is a reimplementation: the code is ours, the content is Nekki's. Every path below
# is either the game's own bytes, something derived from them, or a local working file. A cloner
# regenerates what they need from their own copy of the game with the builders in pvp/tools/.
#
# Verify before the first commit:
#   GIT_DIR=../stage.git GIT_WORK_TREE=. git add -An . | wc -l      # ~120, not 8296
# =============================================================================================

# --- the game's own binaries -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.xapk
sf2_xapk/
unity-re/

# --- assets and data extracted or derived from the game --------------------------------------
extracted/
pvp/data/
pvp/public/atlas/

# --- the reverse-engineering workspace -------------------------------------------------------
# the game's own sf2.js and XML, decompiled class dumps, IL2CPP metadata dumps, string dumps,
# captured frames, third-party community mirrors, and the owner's working notes
re-notes/
rea/
vel-gg/
tmp/
.tmp/

# --- internal working memory -----------------------------------------------------------------
# quotes private messages verbatim and indexes the excluded trees
AGENTS.md

# --- build output and deployment state -------------------------------------------------------
out/
.vercel/
node_modules/
*.log

# --- local tooling and machine-specific helpers ----------------------------------------------
.opencode/
.playwright-mcp/
_probe*.mjs
_hzcheck.mjs
*.ps1

# --- OS / editor -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- not published: keys taken out of the game's own binary ----------------------------------
# pvp/tools/decrypt-textassets.mjs carries AES keys recovered from libil2cpp.so. Whatever its
# use here, publishing it distributes the publisher's own keys and a tool whose only purpose is
# undoing their content protection. That is not source of ours and it does not go in the repo.
pvp/tools/decrypt-textassets.mjs

# the deployment gate passphrase, if you set one (README, "Gating the content paths")
gate.txt
